thinking.text:
Math is rendering as raw `\[\Prob()\]` instead of formatted equations. Kramdown may have converted `$$` delimiters to `\[\]` format.

Inline `$k$` and `$n$` are also rendering as raw text. KaTeX auto-render is likely failing entirely. The cause could be KaTeX not loading, a DMath patch breaking, or a timing issue. Kramdown may have converted `$$` blocks to `\[\]` as plain text.

Repeated patching via setInterval may be nesting wrappers around `katexLoadedCallback`. A guard flag like `DMath._katexMacrosPatched` should prevent duplicate `defineProperty` calls.

Macro persistence requires a shared macros object across every katex.render call. The preamble must be processed explicitly before other math. The `options` getter merges `localOptions` with `DMath.katexOptions`, so macros must remain a single shared reference rather than separate copies.

Object.assign preserves the macros reference, so the shared object is passed correctly to every katex.render call. The real issue is DOM tree order: renderMathInElement processes the preamble div before the \Prob() block because it walks the document tree sequentially. The preamble sits inside a div, which may prevent it from being read as a direct text node.

The raw `\[\Prob()\]` appears outside any `d-math` element, confirming KaTeX never ran. The `\gdef` macro needs `globalGroup: true` to persist globally. The failure could stem from a missing KaTeX load, a syntax error in `\Prob()`, or a broken patch.

Kramdown converts `$$` blocks into `\[` and `\]` delimiters, but the distill script does not recognize those as display math. This explains why the raw `\[\Prob()\]` appears outside any `d-math` element.

The inline `$k$` remains unrendered because KaTeX auto-render never fired. Possible causes include a missing KaTeX script, unset `DMath.katexOptions`, a broken setter patch, or a JavaScript error before the callback.

A specific concern is that `defineProperty` on the `DMath` class may conflict with its static `get` and `set` properties.

The patch may run before the page body parses. Front matter could set `katexOptions` on the original static setter before the patched version exists. If overrides.js loads in the head after template.v2.js, the patch applies early enough to intercept the assignment.

Overrides.js runs synchronously in the head, before the body parses. The plan is to replace `katexLoadedCallback` entirely. It will pre-render `.katex-preamble` elements once KaTeX loads, then invoke the original callback. Afterward it will re-run `renderContent` on every `d-math` tag in DOM order. A single shared macros object will live at the module level in overrides.

A cleaner approach replaces the `defineProperty` hack entirely. A shared macros object will be stored on `window` as `__DISTILL_KATEX_MACROS__`. The patched `katexLoadedCallback` will assign this shared object to `DMath._katexOptions.macros` and enable `globalGroup: true` before invoking the original callback. It will also preprocess `.katex-preamble` elements by extracting their `$$` content and rendering it first.

The cleanest fix is to override `DMath.prototype.renderContent` directly. This ensures every `d-math` instance receives the shared macros object and `globalGroup: true` automatically, without relying on `defineProperty` or `Object.assign` in the options getter.

